// spec: a C function is one function whatever namespace declares it (C++ [dcl.link] 6), so two declarations of one C name with two types are an error, never two overloads a call chooses between: the library's C declarations as the headers have them (library/c_declarations_as_in_c_headers)
// error: the C function kppSpecTwice is declared with two types
extern "C" int kppSpecTwice(int value);
namespace other
{
  extern "C" int kppSpecTwice(double value);
}
int main()
{
  return 0;
}